From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 45/55] kex: do not leave a freed cipher name in newkeys

When kex_choose_conf() promotes the serial ChaCha20-Poly1305 cipher to the
multithreaded one it frees newkeys->enc.name and then looks the new cipher up.
If that lookup failed the code jumped to the error exit with the name freed but
still set, and freeing newkeys would free it again. Clear the pointer after the
free. The lookup cannot fail while the name is in my[nenc], so this is only a
guard.
---
 kex.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kex.c b/kex.c
index 07790fd06..4edbfc362 100644
--- a/kex.c
+++ b/kex.c
@@ -1158,6 +1158,9 @@ kex_choose_conf(struct ssh *ssh, uint32_t seq)
 			 * multithreaded implementation is an option...
 			 */
 			free(newkeys->enc.name);
+			/* not left pointing at what was freed: the error path
+			 * below frees newkeys, name and all */
+			newkeys->enc.name = NULL;
 			newkeys->enc.cipher = cipher_by_name(
 			    "chacha20-poly1305-mt@hpnssh.org");
 			if (newkeys->enc.cipher == NULL) {
